  shipped as a deck. WHICH LADDER IS THE HEADLINE (this 550-d spec ladder or the 240-d Q&A schedule of
  ms33_modelVII_freeswelling.prj): RULED 2026-09-12 (Vinay: keep both variants of model vii): both ladders
  registered and reported, neither is the headline.
  LINEAGE: the parent deck's 240-d step-and-hold schedule (0.1-d ramps, 5-d holds, Questions.tex R23/R27) is kept
  in the traction_ramp curve comment below as the superseded-for-this-deck curve.

Traction sign convention: compression = negative (σ_zz < 0 → traction t_z < 0).
Curve traction_ramp gives the Neumann z-traction on the top face.

IC note: Initial suction is kept benchmark-compliant at 100 MPa.
For consistency with the benchmark-aligned Pi-path initialization used in Models I/III/IV,
initial micro water content is set to the 99 MPa-equilibrium value.
