       live-K switch, three parallel runs {80x, 160x, 320x} showed 320x plateauing
       EXACTLY flat from 100 d onward (e_top identical at 100/150/200 d = 1.13705,
       a converged asymptote), 80x sitting 0.83 percent short of that asymptote AT
       the 200 d horizon itself (no safety margin; fails the same standard that
       rejected III's 100x), and 160x matching the 320x asymptote to 0.015 percent
       with Aitken-extrapolated t_eq(1 percent) <= 100 d, i.e. a >=100-day safety
       margin (measured, this session; see DSM/AGENTS.md for the dated entry).
       REASON, same mechanism as Model III (DSM/AGENTS.md section 7): macro
       saturation collapses to ~0, so relative_permeability sits pinned on its
       1e-2 floor throughout, making the effective conductivity k0*1e-2; the
       acceleration compensates for that, it is not a change of physics.
       NO RADIAL CONFINEMENT (Vinay 2026-08-17, checked against spec and
       cross-team descriptions: CIMNE-UPC treats a confined VII as a separate
       ADDITIONAL exercise, UCLM's own VII assumes radial confinement, teams
       disagree; kept unconfined per Vinay's explicit call, DSM/AGENTS.md
       section 14). -->
